<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's NLCF buys 43,500 tonnes cottonseed meal.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's NLCF buys 43,500 tonnes cottonseed meal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's National Livestock Cooperatives Federation (NLCF) said on Wednesday it bought 24,000 tonnes of Chinese cottonseed meal and 19,500 tonnes of Australian cottonseed meal.  </p>
<p>An NLCF official said it also passed on tenders for 6,500 tonnes due to high prices.</p>
<p>NLCF will re-invite the tenders on Friday.</p>
<p>The official said it bought 24,000 tonnes of Chinese cottonseed meal from LG International Corp and bought 19,500 tonnes from Cargill with Australian origin.</p>
<p>Details for the tender results are as follows:</p>
<p> POSITION  TONNE   ETA	ARRIVAL PORT  PRICE     SELLER</p>
<p>  One	6,500   July 10  Inchon	  $166	Cargill</p>
<p>  Two	3,500   July 30  Kunsan/Ulsan  $161.50   LG</p>
<p>  Three    6,500   Aug 10   Inchon	  $161.50   LG</p>
<p>  Four     3,500   Aug 30   Kunsan/Ulsan  $162.50   LG</p>
<p>  Five     6,500   Sep 10   Inchon	  $169	Cargill</p>
<p>  Six	3,500   Sep 30   Kunsan/Ulsan  $165	LG</p>
<p>  Seven    6,500   Oct 10   Inchon	  PASSED</p>
<p>  Eight    3,500   Oct 10   Kunsan/Ulsan  $167	LG</p>
<p>  Nine     6,500   Nov 10   Inchon	  $173	Cargill</p>
<p>  Ten	3,500   Nov 10   Kunsan/Ulsan  $168	LG</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
